-- ---- body MOVE events (bulk transform readback; 1-based) ----
/**
Summary: Snapshot every body that moved in the last step.

pWorld: The world handle.

Returns: The number of bodies that moved.

Example:
repeat with i = 1 to b2BodiesUpdate(tWorld)
   put b2BodyMoveBody(i), b2BodyMoveX(i), b2BodyMoveY(i) & cr after tMoves
end repeat

Description:
Call it once after each <b2Step>. One call gathers the new transform of
every moved body, which is far cheaper than asking each body with
<b2BodyX>. Sleeping bodies do not appear. A stale world clears the
snapshot and returns 0.

References: b2BodyMoveBody (handler), b2BodyMoveX (handler),
b2BodyMoveFellAsleep (handler)
*/
public handler b2BodiesUpdate(in pWorld as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _bodies_update(pWorld) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return how many bodies the move snapshot holds.

Returns: The count from the last <b2BodiesUpdate>.

