pWake: true to wake the body if it sleeps.

Example:
b2ApplyForceAt tBody, 0, 20, b2BodyX(tBody) + 1, b2BodyY(tBody), true

Description:
Off the centre of mass the force also turns the body. Apply it every
step for as long as it should push. A non-finite value is ignored. A
stale or 0 handle is a harmless no-op.

References: b2ApplyForce (handler), b2ApplyImpulseAt (handler)
*/
public handler b2ApplyForceAt(in pBody as Integer, in pFx as Number, in pFy as Number, in pPointX as Number, in pPointY as Number, in pWake as Boolean)
   unsafe
      _body_apply_force_at(pBody, pFx, pFy, pPointX, pPointY, bi(pWake))
   end unsafe
end handler

