pIx: The x component of the impulse in newton-seconds.

pIy: The y component of the impulse in newton-seconds.

pPointX: The x of the point of application in world metres.

pPointY: The y of the point of application in world metres.

pWake: true to wake the body if it sleeps.

Example:
b2ApplyImpulseAt tBody, 3, 0, tHitX, tHitY, true

Description:
Off the centre of mass the impulse also sets the body spinning. A
non-finite value is ignored. A stale or 0 handle is a harmless no-op.

References: b2ApplyImpulse (handler), b2ApplyForceAt (handler)
*/
public handler b2ApplyImpulseAt(in pBody as Integer, in pIx as Number, in pIy as Number, in pPointX as Number, in pPointY as Number, in pWake as Boolean)
