/**
Summary: Override a body's mass, centre of mass and inertia.

pBody: The body handle.

pMass: The mass in kilograms, 0 or more.

pCenterX: The x of the centre of mass in the body's local frame, in
metres.

pCenterY: The y of the centre of mass in the body's local frame, in
metres.

pInertia: The rotational inertia about the centre of mass, in kg m^2, 0
or more.

Example:
b2SetMassData tBody, 5, 0, -0.3, 0.8

Description:
Adding or changing shapes later can recompute the mass from the shapes
again; <b2ApplyMassFromShapes> does that on purpose. The call is ignored
when the mass or inertia is negative or a value is not finite. A stale
or 0 handle is a harmless no-op.

References: b2ApplyMassFromShapes (handler),
b2BodyMassDataUpdate (handler)
*/
public handler b2SetMassData(in pBody as Integer, in pMass as Number, in pCenterX as Number, in pCenterY as Number, in pInertia as Number)
   unsafe
      _body_set_mass_data(pBody, pMass, pCenterX, pCenterY, pInertia)
   end unsafe
end handler

/**
Summary: Recompute a body's mass from its shapes.

pBody: The body handle.

Example:
b2ApplyMassFromShapes tBody

Description:
Undoes a <b2SetMassData> override. A stale or 0 handle is a harmless
no-op.

References: b2SetMassData (handler)
*/
public handler b2ApplyMassFromShapes(in pBody as Integer)
   unsafe
      _body_apply_mass_from_shapes(pBody)
   end unsafe
end handler

/**
Summary: Drive a kinematic body to reach a pose after a time step.

pBody: The body handle.

pX: The target x in metres.

pY: The target y in metres.

pAngle: The target angle in radians.

pTimeStep: The time in seconds to get there, usually the next step's
length; must be above 0.

Example:
b2SetTargetTransform tPlatform, tNextX, tNextY, 0, 1/60

Description:
Box2D sets the body's velocities so it arrives at the pose, so it pushes
other bodies properly on the way, unlike the teleport of
<b2SetTransform>. Use it on kinematic bodies. The call is ignored when
the time step is not above 0 or a value is not finite. A stale or 0
handle is a harmless no-op.

References: b2SetTransform (handler), b2NewKinematicBody (handler)
*/
public handler b2SetTargetTransform(in pBody as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number, in pAngle as Number, in pTimeStep as Number)
   unsafe
      _body_set_target_transform(pBody, pX, pY, pAngle, pTimeStep)
   end unsafe
end handler

