/**
Summary: Change a shape's collision filter.

pShape: The shape handle.

pCategory: The category bits this shape belongs to (0 to 2^53-1).

pMask: The category bits it collides with (0 to 2^53-1).

pGroup: The group index: a shared positive group always collides, a
shared negative group never does; 0 means none.

Example:
b2SetShapeFilter tShape, 4, 1, 0

Description:
The whole call is ignored when the category or mask is out of range or
not finite. A default mask reads back as 2^64-1, so clamp it before
writing it back; xTalk's bitAnd and bitOr are 32-bit anyway. A stale or
0 handle is a harmless no-op.

References: b2ShapeFilterCategory (handler),
b2ShapeFilterMask (handler), b2ShapeDefFilter (handler)
*/
