-- ---- world queries (overlap / ray-cast-all / shape-cast); results 1-based ----
/**
Summary: Find every shape whose bounding box overlaps a rectangle.

pWorld: The world handle.

pX1: The x of one corner in world metres.

pY1: The y of that corner.

pX2: The x of the opposite corner.

pY2: The y of the opposite corner.

Returns: The number of shapes found.

Example:
repeat with i = 1 to b2OverlapAABB(tWorld, 0, 0, 10, 5)
   put b2QueryBody(i) & cr after tFound
end repeat

Description:
The corners may be given in any order. The test is against each shape's
bounding box, so it can include shapes that only come close. The rows
carry no point or normal. Each query clears the shared result rows and
returns how many it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>, <b2QueryShape>
and the other b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world returns 0.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2QueryBody (handler),
b2OverlapCircle (handler)
*/
public handler b2OverlapAABB(in pWorld as Integer, in pX1 as Number, in pY1 as Number, in pX2 as Number, in pY2 as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_overlap_aabb(pWorld, pX1, pY1, pX2, pY2) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Find every shape that contains a world point.

pWorld: The world handle.

pX: The x of the point in world metres.

pY: The y of the point in world metres.

Returns: The number of shapes found.

Example:
repeat with i = 1 to b2OverlapPoint(tWorld, tX, tY)
   put b2QueryShape(i) & cr after tUnder
end repeat

Description:
Each row's point is the query point; it has no normal or fraction.
<b2BodyAtPoint> is the single-result form. Each query clears the shared
result rows and returns how many it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>,
<b2QueryShape> and the other b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world
returns 0.

References: b2BodyAtPoint (handler), b2QueryShape (handler)
*/
public handler b2OverlapPoint(in pWorld as Integer, in pX as Number, in pY as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_overlap_point(pWorld, pX, pY) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Find every shape that overlaps a circle.

pWorld: The world handle.

pCx: The x of the centre in world metres.

pCy: The y of the centre in world metres.

pRadius: The radius in metres.

Returns: The number of shapes found.

Example:
repeat with i = 1 to b2OverlapCircle(tWorld, tX, tY, 3)
   b2ApplyImpulse b2QueryBody(i), 0, 2, true
end repeat

Description:
The rows carry no point or normal. Each query clears the shared result
rows and returns how many it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>,
<b2QueryShape> and the other b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world
returns 0.

References: b2OverlapShape (handler), b2QueryBody (handler)
*/
public handler b2OverlapCircle(in pWorld as Integer, in pCx as Number, in pCy as Number, in pRadius as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_overlap_circle(pWorld, pCx, pCy, pRadius) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Find every shape that overlaps a shape built from the vertex builder.

pWorld: The world handle.

pRadius: A rounding radius added around the points, in metres (0 for
sharp corners).

Returns: The number of shapes found; 0 when the vertex builder is empty.

Example:
b2PolyBegin
b2PolyAddPoint 0, 0
b2PolyAddPoint 2, 0
b2PolyAddPoint 1, 2
put b2OverlapShape(tWorld, 0) into tCount

Description:
Add the points in world coordinates with <b2PolyBegin> and
<b2PolyAddPoint>; one point with a radius is a circle, two make a
capsule. The rows carry no point or normal. Each query clears the shared
result rows and returns how many it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>,
<b2QueryShape> and the other b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world
returns 0.

References: b2PolyBegin (handler), b2ShapeCast (handler),
b2QueryShape (handler)
*/
public handler b2OverlapShape(in pWorld as Integer, in pRadius as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_overlap_shape(pWorld, pRadius) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Find every shape along a ray, nearest first.

pWorld: The world handle.

pX1: The x of the start point in world metres.

pY1: The y of the start point.

pX2: The x of the end point.

pY2: The y of the end point.

Returns: The number of hits.

Example:
repeat with i = 1 to b2RayCastAll(tWorld, 0, 0, 20, 0)
   put b2QueryX(i), b2QueryY(i) & cr after tHits
end repeat

Description:
The rows are sorted by fraction, near to far, and each carries the hit
point, normal and fraction. For just the closest hit use
<b2CastRayClosest>. Each query clears the shared result rows and returns
how many it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>, <b2QueryShape> and the
other b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world returns 0.

References: b2CastRayClosest (handler), b2QueryFraction (handler),
b2QueryX (handler)
*/
public handler b2RayCastAll(in pWorld as Integer, in pX1 as Number, in pY1 as Number, in pX2 as Number, in pY2 as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_raycast_all(pWorld, pX1, pY1, pX2, pY2) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Sweep a shape from the vertex builder through a world and gather the hits.

pWorld: The world handle.

pRadius: A rounding radius added around the points, in metres.

pDx: The x of the sweep's translation in metres.

pDy: The y of the sweep's translation in metres.

Returns: The number of hits; 0 when the vertex builder is empty.

Example:
b2PolyBegin
b2PolyAddPoint tX, tY
put b2ShapeCast(tWorld, 0.5, 0, -10) into tCount
if tCount > 0 then put b2QueryFraction(1) into tFirst

Description:
Builds a proxy from the points added with <b2PolyBegin> and
<b2PolyAddPoint> (world coordinates) and moves it by the translation.
The rows are sorted near to far and carry the hit point, normal and
fraction. Each query clears the shared result rows and returns how many
it found; read them with <b2QueryBody>, <b2QueryShape> and the other
b2Query handlers (1-based). A stale world returns 0.

References: b2PolyBegin (handler), b2OverlapShape (handler),
b2QueryFraction (handler)
*/
public handler b2ShapeCast(in pWorld as Integer, in pRadius as Number, in pDx as Number, in pDy as Number) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_shapecast(pWorld, pRadius, pDx, pDy) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return how many rows the last world query found.

Returns: The row count.

Example:
put b2QueryCount() into tCount

Description:
The same number the query returned.

References: b2OverlapAABB (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2QueryBody (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryCount() returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_count() into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the body of a query row.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

Returns: A body handle, or 0 when the index is out of range.

Example:
put b2QueryBody(1) into tValue

Description:
Reads the rows of the last world query.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2OverlapAABB (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryBody(in pIndex as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_body(pIndex - 1) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the shape of a query row.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

Returns: A shape handle, or 0 when the index is out of range.

Example:
put b2QueryShape(1) into tValue

Description:
Reads the rows of the last world query.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2OverlapAABB (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryShape(in pIndex as Integer) returns Integer
   variable tR as Integer
   unsafe
      put _query_shape(pIndex - 1) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the x of a query row's point.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

Returns: The x in world metres, or 0 when the index is out of range.

Example:
put b2QueryX(1) into tValue

Description:
Reads the rows of the last world query. Filled by the ray and shape
casts and by <b2OverlapPoint>; the other overlaps leave it 0.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2OverlapAABB (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryX(in pIndex as Integer) returns Number
   variable tR as Number
   unsafe
      put _query_x(pIndex - 1) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the y of a query row's point.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

Returns: The y in world metres, or 0 when the index is out of range.

Example:
put b2QueryY(1) into tValue

Description:
Reads the rows of the last world query. Filled by the ray and shape
casts and by <b2OverlapPoint>; the other overlaps leave it 0.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2OverlapAABB (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryY(in pIndex as Integer) returns Number
   variable tR as Number
   unsafe
      put _query_y(pIndex - 1) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the x of a query row's surface normal.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

Returns: The normal's x component, or 0 when the index is out of range.

Example:
put b2QueryNormalX(1) into tValue

Description:
Reads the rows of the last world query. Filled only by <b2RayCastAll>
and <b2ShapeCast>.

References: b2QueryCount (handler), b2RayCastAll (handler),
b2OverlapAABB (handler)
*/
public handler b2QueryNormalX(in pIndex as Integer) returns Number
   variable tR as Number
   unsafe
      put _query_normal_x(pIndex - 1) into tR
   end unsafe
   return tR
end handler

/**
Summary: Return the y of a query row's surface normal.

pIndex: The 1-based row index, from 1 to <b2QueryCount>.

